'''Raids''' are group activities for [[members]] in which the goal of the player(s) is to defeat several bosses in a row, often without banking, before facing the final boss of the raid. When the final boss is defeated, players can claim their rewards from a chest. As raids are intended for endgame accounts, the rewards from raids are very lucrative and generally considered the best in their category. Raids possess numerous unique drops, but the most prized drops, known as "mega rares", are some of the strongest weapons players can possess.

Due to the high-level nature of raids, players are expected to bring equipment to cover the entire [[combat triangle]].

All raids take place in an instance, with the [[Chambers of Xeric]] (barring [[Chambers of Xeric/Challenge Mode|Challenge Mode]]) having a randomly generated arrangement. All three raids have a hard mode variant to them, and the [[Theatre of Blood]] and [[Tombs of Amascut]] both have easier, entry mode variants as well.<!--Tombs of Amascut expert can be considered hard mode-->

Raids scale based on the following:

*Chambers of Xeric - party size's overall combat stats determine the health and combat levels of enemies in the encounter, while party's overall skill stats determines resources and skill challenge requirements.
*Theatre of Blood - party size determines overall health of enemies in raid - if attempted in a solo or duo scale, enemies' health is scaled to trio scale.
*Tombs of Amascut - active raid invocations determines overall combat stats and health of enemies in raid. Party size, in groups higher than solo scale, also determine enemies' health.

When completing a raid, multiple rolls are made on the normal drop table. If a unique item is received during a raid, the interacting item will have a purple indicator of some form instead.

Raids can be identified with a brown star {{SCP|raid}} [[icon]] on the [[World map|map]].

==List of raids==
There are currently three raids, the [[Chambers of Xeric]], the [[Theatre of Blood]], and the [[Tombs of Amascut]]. Each one features its own unique mechanics that make the three raids very different in practice to one another, with different balances of combat, puzzles, and skilling encounters, as well as different amounts of customisability and difficulty levels.

A fourth raid, [[The Fractured Archive]], is planned to be released around late 2026.

